ing about politics and history at  the same time that you're actually  experiencing it in your day to day  internship and that combination of  things makes for great learning anyone  no matter where they want to end up  after college can benefit from spending  a semester in Washington DC the  experiences you have here the classes  you take here the people you meet here  they will help you no matter where you  end up these people they really can  change your future and get you to where  you want to be I get a lot of resumes  across my desk when you look at a resume  you see pretty much the same thing over  and over it when we find somebody coming  out of college who has some practical  real-world experience it really sets  them apart those are the people we  interviewed the Kirby Center has  produced some of the best interns we  have found in all of the years that both  congressman McClintock and I have been  on Capitol Hill that's why we look to  them we know that the insurance they  send leave an indelible mark on this  office I have to look at the larger  picture about investing in your future  and that's what I feel like I'm doing  here and it's given me a lot of guidance  to what I'm gonna do after Hillsdale  that's very important it's coming up  sooner than you would think it just  really changed their life because they  now see what they learned on campus  those principals ideas put into practice  they see them alive in Washington DC  it's a transformative experience so  you've just got to take the leap of  faith and push yourself and push your  education to the next logical step come  to Washington DC
 

